<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serfoji II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1777–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Serfoji II of Thanjavur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Serfoji II was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> raja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1798 to 1832. In 1799 he ceded the administration of his kingdom to the British, keeping the fort and an income. Educated by the missionary Christian Friedrich Schwartz, he devoted himself to learning, enlarging the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saraswati">Saraswati</a> Mahal library and patronising Carnatic music, Tanjore painting and an early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/serfoji-ii.jpg" alt="Serfoji II" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serfoji_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
